      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Idol: one image to a 3D Gaussian splat\n\n**First run** downloads the Idol weights (~3 GB) to `models/idol/` and DINOv3 to the Hugging Face cache. DINOv3 is gated: accept its terms on Hugging Face and log in with `hf auth login`.\n\n**Model Loader**: `flux2_vae_source` points to FLUX.2 klein, which is not gated and has the same VAE as FLUX.2-dev.\n\n**Input image**\n- PNG with transparency: keep the `MASK` link and `invert_mask` on. Load Image stores alpha inverted, and the toggle undoes that.\n- JPG or an image without alpha: delete the `MASK` link (or leave it, an empty mask is ignored). BiRefNet removes the background.\n\n**mode**: `synthetic` for renders and generated images, `real` for photos.\n\n**num_gaussians**: 32,768 to 1,048,576. More is sharper and slower to view.\n\n**fast_sampling**: batched CFG + cuDNN attention. Turn it off if VRAM is low.\n\n**Output**: the `.ply` goes to `output/idol/`. Preview Splat shows it in the graph. Connect `model_3d` to *Get Splat* for the other core splat nodes (render, transform, splat to mesh)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
